                <pb facs="0822" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg700"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Claparède to
                        Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Switzerland</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 27, 1888</date>.
                        (Received November 27.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: In pursuance of instructions
                    received from my Government, I have the honor to inform you that Mr.
                    Hertenstein, President of the Swiss Confederation, last night succumbed to the
                    effects of the operation performed on Saturday last.</p>
                <p>Begging you, Mr. Secretary, to communicate the intelligence of this sad and
                    painful event to the President of the United States of America,</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. de Claparède.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
